{
"content_id": "23157",
"reference_id": 22325,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "Philemon 1:2",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "57001002",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<ul><li><p>This letter is not just for Philemon, it is also for his family and the church that met in their home. </p></li><li><p>Apphia was probably Philemon’s wife.</p></li><li><p><em>our fellow soldier</em>: This refers to a servant of Christ who is in a spiritual battle and must be ready to fight against challenges (<a href=\"https://ref.ly/Eph6:10-Eph6:17\">Ephesians 6:10–17</a>).</p></li><li><p>Archippus was probably Philemon’s son (also mentioned in <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Col4:17\">Colossians 4:17</a>). </p></li><li><p><em>the church that meets in your house</em>: This confirms that some early Christians would gather in private homes for worship (see also <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Rom16:5\">Romans 16:5</a>; <a href=\"https://ref.ly/1Cor16:19\">1 Corinthians 16:19</a>; <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Col4:15\">Colossians 4:15</a>).</p></li></ul>",
"associations": {
"passage": [
{
"start_ref": "57001002",
"start_ref_usfm": "PHM 1:2",
"end_ref": "57001002",
"end_ref_usfm": "PHM 1:2"
}
