"content_id": "23162",
"reference_id": 22330,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "Philemon 1:8–9",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "57001008-57001009",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<ul><li><p>The apostle Paul asked for a favor because Philemon was well-known as a kind and loving person (<a href=\"https://ref.ly/Phlm1:5-Phlm1:7\">1:5–7</a>). Paul could have used his authority as an apostle of Christ to demand it, but he chose to ask out of love.</p></li><li><p><span><em>I, Paul, am now aged</em></span>: Paul appealed to the respect owed to older people and his status as <em>a prisoner for Christ Jesus</em>, which would increase a fellow Christian’s respect.</p></li></ul>",
"associations": {
