"title": "Philemon 1:11",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "57001011",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<ul><li><p>Onesimus means “useful.” </p></li><li><p><span><em>Formerly he was useless, but now he has become useful</em></span>: This might be a play on words (compare <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Phlm1:20\">1:20</a>). Onesimus was now serving others and sharing the good news about Jesus. At last he had become what his name means.</p></li></ul>",
"associations": {
