"title": "Philemon 1:20",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "57001020",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<p><span><em>let me have some benefit</em>:</span> Or do <em>me this favor</em>. The Greek word <em>onaimēn</em> (meaning “favor” or “benefit”) may be a wordplay on the name Onesimus, which can mean “useful” or “beneficial” (compare <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Phlm1:11\">1:11</a>).</p>",
