"title": "Philemon 1:24",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "57001024",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<ul><li><p>Paul mentions these men at the end of his letter to the Colossians (<a href=\"https://ref.ly/Col4:10\">Colossians 4:10</a>, <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Col4:14\">14</a>). </p></li><li><p><em>fellow workers</em>: They helped the apostle Paul spread the good news about Jesus.</p></li><li><p><em>Mark</em>: See “<span data-bnType=\"resourceReference\" data-resourceId=\"203502\" data-resourceType=\"TyndaleStudyNotesProfiles\">John Mark</span>” Profile.</p></li><li><p><em>Aristarchus: </em>He was a faithful helper who served with Paul for many years (<a href=\"https://ref.ly/Acts19:29\">Acts 19:29</a>; <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Acts20:4\">20:4</a>; <a href=\"https://ref.ly/Acts27:2\">27:2</a>).</p></li><li><p><em>Demas</em>: He was a fellow worker who later abandoned Paul (<a href=\"https://ref.ly/2Tim4:10\">2&nbsp;Timothy 4:10</a>).</p></li><li><p><em>Luke</em>: See “<span data-bnType=\"resourceReference\" data-resourceId=\"203504\" data-resourceType=\"TyndaleStudyNotesProfiles\">Luke</span>” Profile.</p></li></ul>",
